python3 ./unixnu build payload -D ../UniXNU-instantnoodlep \
  --unique-chip-id 0123456789abcdef \
  --trust-cache out/ipsw/21H461/trust.bundle
  -> payload/payload.img  92,274,688 bytes (88 MiB)
     trust bundle sha256 7416ca4f8377146626bb284e2133c76bee6cb4e3ee0af5d648b186235a7323a7
     (built by scripts/bundle-ipsw-trust.py from the two 21H461 modules)

python3 ./unixnu bootimg -D ../UniXNU-instantnoodlep --uefi ../uefi-instantnoodlep \
  --dtb ../uefi-instantnoodlep/Resources/DTBs/instantnoodlep.dtb
  -> boot/boot.img  94,339,072 bytes  sha256 2d6158277e87ce1885de31870a3598135b60a419cb2b145318fb845bbcd5c8df
     header v1, pagesize 4096, ramdisk_bytes 92,274,688
     fd_sha256    188a52f64d33b1a24e6cabea70cbec1088b5d76a9c2125b7a29b7d99e7840c32
     dtb_sha256   f7fa0c06d6719bd9a04f3a39be7fd117a527ced59904b5c76da8ae37c5de27f7
     shim_bytes   112

Note: the platform seed above is a placeholder, so the image proves packing, not
production identity. The local UniXNU checkout carries a one-line workaround in
scripts/unixnu/bootimg.py: the integrated assembler leaves the BootShim
image_size field as FD_SIZE only, and llvm-objcopy cannot resolve the
_Payload-_Head relocation, so the field is rewritten to len(shim)+FD_SIZE.
